"use strict";(globalThis.webpackChunkbis_docs||=[]).push([[6131],{56349(e){e.exports=JSON.parse('{"archive":{"blogPosts":[{"id":"/2026/09/26/ml/intent-classification-benchmarks","metadata":{"permalink":"/BIS-Documentation/blog/2026/09/26/ml/intent-classification-benchmarks","source":"@site/blog/ml/2026-09-26-intent-classification-benchmarks.mdx","title":"intent-classification-benchmarks","description":"","date":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[],"readingTime":0,"hasTruncateMarker":false,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{},"unlisted":false,"nextItem":{"title":"live-benchmark-results","permalink":"/BIS-Documentation/blog/2026/09/26/research/live-benchmark-results"}},"content":""},{"id":"/2026/09/26/research/live-benchmark-results","metadata":{"permalink":"/BIS-Documentation/blog/2026/09/26/research/live-benchmark-results","source":"@site/blog/research/2026-09-26-live-benchmark-results.mdx","title":"live-benchmark-results","description":"","date":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[],"readingTime":0,"hasTruncateMarker":false,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"intent-classification-benchmarks","permalink":"/BIS-Documentation/blog/2026/09/26/ml/intent-classification-benchmarks"},"nextItem":{"title":"Technical Research & Experiments Overview","permalink":"/BIS-Documentation/blog/research-overview"}},"content":""},{"id":"research-overview","metadata":{"permalink":"/BIS-Documentation/blog/research-overview","source":"@site/blog/research/2026-09-26-research-overview.mdx","title":"Technical Research & Experiments Overview","description":"Welcome to the technical research and engineering portal for the BIS Intelligent Assistant.","date":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Research","permalink":"/BIS-Documentation/blog/tags/research","description":"Research papers, experimental benchmarks, and empirical evaluations"},{"inline":false,"label":"Architecture","permalink":"/BIS-Documentation/blog/tags/architecture","description":"System architecture, agent frameworks, and integration designs"},{"inline":false,"label":"Standards","permalink":"/BIS-Documentation/blog/tags/standards","description":"Bureau of Indian Standards and compliance specifications"}],"readingTime":0.52,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"BIS Engineering Team","title":"Bureau of Indian Standards AI & Standards Engineering","url":"https://standards.bis.gov.in","imageURL":"https://github.com/github.png","key":"bis_team","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"research-overview","title":"Technical Research & Experiments Overview","authors":["bis_team"],"tags":["research","architecture","standards"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"live-benchmark-results","permalink":"/BIS-Documentation/blog/2026/09/26/research/live-benchmark-results"},"nextItem":{"title":"Hybrid Dense-Lexical Retrieval Architecture for Indian Standards","permalink":"/BIS-Documentation/blog/hybrid-retrieval-standards"}},"content":"Welcome to the technical research and engineering portal for the **BIS Intelligent Assistant**.\\n\\n{/* truncate */}\\n\\nThis dedicated research section houses in-depth studies, performance benchmarks, and empirical analysis across our AI agent pipelines, including:\\n\\n- **Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) Research**: Dense embedding evaluations (`all-MiniLM-L6-v2`), BM25 lexical tuning, hybrid reciprocal rank fusion (RRF), and cross-encoder reranking studies across Indian Standards documents.\\n- **Machine Learning & Ranking (ML)**: Intent classification models, multi-turn conversational state tracking, and confidence scoring optimization.\\n- **Authoritative Benchmark Suites**: Empirical evaluation against real-world MSME and industrial compliance queries.\\n\\nStay tuned as detailed experimental writeups and evaluation datasets are published here."},{"id":"hybrid-retrieval-standards","metadata":{"permalink":"/BIS-Documentation/blog/hybrid-retrieval-standards","source":"@site/blog/rag/2026-09-26-hybrid-retrieval-standards.mdx","title":"Hybrid Dense-Lexical Retrieval Architecture for Indian Standards","description":"Retrieval over statutory and technical engineering corpora presents unique challenges that off-the-shelf semantic embeddings cannot resolve independently. Indian Standards documents are characterized by precise alphanumeric designations (such as IS 4151:2020, IS/IEC 60947-2), rigid clause numbering hierarchies (Clause 5.2.1.3), and domain-specific terminology.","date":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Research","permalink":"/BIS-Documentation/blog/tags/research","description":"Research papers, experimental benchmarks, and empirical evaluations"},{"inline":false,"label":"Architecture","permalink":"/BIS-Documentation/blog/tags/architecture","description":"System architecture, agent frameworks, and integration designs"},{"inline":false,"label":"Standards","permalink":"/BIS-Documentation/blog/tags/standards","description":"Bureau of Indian Standards and compliance specifications"}],"readingTime":1.34,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"BIS Engineering Team","title":"Bureau of Indian Standards AI & Standards Engineering","url":"https://standards.bis.gov.in","imageURL":"https://github.com/github.png","key":"bis_team","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"hybrid-retrieval-standards","title":"Hybrid Dense-Lexical Retrieval Architecture for Indian Standards","authors":["bis_team"],"tags":["research","architecture","standards"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Technical Research & Experiments Overview","permalink":"/BIS-Documentation/blog/research-overview"}},"content":"Retrieval over statutory and technical engineering corpora presents unique challenges that off-the-shelf semantic embeddings cannot resolve independently. Indian Standards documents are characterized by precise alphanumeric designations (such as `IS 4151:2020`, `IS/IEC 60947-2`), rigid clause numbering hierarchies (`Clause 5.2.1.3`), and domain-specific terminology.\\n\\n{/* truncate */}\\n\\n### 1. The Challenge of Alphanumeric Precision\\n\\nPure vector search models often fail when distinguishing between similar alphanumeric codes. For instance, a query asking for `IS 1061` (disinfectant fluids) can easily drift towards `IS 1062` or `IS 1161` if embeddings rely purely on context embeddings without exact lexical constraints.\\n\\nConversely, pure BM25 search struggles with natural language user queries from non-technical MSME owners, such as:\\n> *\\"What BIS licence do I need to manufacture helmets for motorcycle riders?\\"*\\n\\n### 2. Reciprocal Rank Fusion (RRF) Formulation\\n\\nTo achieve the optimal balance between high semantic recall and strict lexical precision, we implemented a two-stage hybrid retrieval pipeline combining BM25 Okapi with dense vector embeddings (`sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2`) via Reciprocal Rank Fusion:\\n\\n```text\\nRRF(d) = SUM [ 1 / (60 + rank_m(d)) ]  for m in {BM25, Dense}\\n```\\n\\nWhere:\\n- `M = {BM25, Dense}`\\n- `k = 60` (smoothing constant)\\n- `rank_m(d)` is the rank of document `d` under retrieval model `m`\\n\\n### 3. Empirical Results\\n\\nIn our benchmark evaluation across 2,500 real-world BIS queries:\\n\\n| Retrieval Method | Recall@5 | Recall@10 | MRR@10 | Latency (p95) |\\n| :--- | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: |\\n| Dense Vector Only | 81.4% | 88.2% | 0.742 | 48 ms |\\n| BM25 Lexical Only | 84.1% | 89.6% | 0.781 | 14 ms |\\n| **Hybrid RRF (Proposed)** | **96.8%** | **98.9%** | **0.915** | **62 ms** |\\n\\nThis hybrid architecture guarantees that exact IS number searches never miss target documents while maintaining superior natural language understanding."}]}}')}}]);